# Stage 2 — internal PHP and JS identifiers.
#
# Everything here appears only in PHP and JS inside this plugin. None of it is
# a database key, a PHP filter or action, a JS hook, a jQuery event, a request
# field, a CSS selector, an element id, a class in emitted markup, or a file
# name. .tools/rename-plan.py checks every one of those channels and these came
# back with none of them. None of the eight add-ons references any of them.
#
# Deliberately excluded, each to the stage that owns its real channel:
#
#   * 44 identifiers ending in "_" are concatenation prefixes, and the name
#     that reaches the runtime belongs elsewhere — 'gform_wrapper_' . $id is a
#     DOM id, 'gform_submit_button_' . $id is a filter name, 'gf_dimissed_' .
#     $key is an option key.
#   * 78 that looked internal but are JS hook names (gform.addAction) or jQuery
#     event names, including gform_post_render — the event every custom script
#     on the site binds to. The classifier only knew about PHP hooks until this
#     stage; it knows about both JS channels now.
#   * gf_step_first/_last/_next/_pending/_previous, gform_card_icon_inactive,
#     gform_legacy_markup and gform_validation_error_link, which JS adds with
#     addClass, so they are markup.
#
# gform_ -> kform_, gforms_ -> kforms_, gf_ -> kdna_, except for four that the
# audit already reports as live mismatches. For those the correct target is the
# name the other side of the plugin is already using, so they are merged rather
# than prefixed — renaming them to kform_ would only move the mismatch:
#
#   gf_apply_rules                  JS calls kdnaform_apply_rules()
#   gform_initialize_tooltips       JS calls kdnaform_initialize_tooltips()
#   gform_payment_method_creditcard PHP emits id=kdnaform_payment_method_creditcard
#   gform_predefined_choices        PHP emits var kdnaform_predefined_choices

